'''
Toxiproxy test extension.

Launch a toxiproxy-server daemon and drive it with toxiproxy-cli so that tests
can inject transport-level network conditions (latency, bandwidth, connection
resets, partitions) on any loopback TCP leg of an AuTest topology -- for
example the ATS -> origin or ATS -> parent leg. This complements Proxy Verifier,
which models HTTP-level behavior (status, headers, response delay) but not
TCP-level faults such as resets, bandwidth caps, or blackhole partitions.
'''
